sses. This allowed the Allies to design aircraft to measure up to the Zero, which resulted in the design of the Grummen Hellcat.","LocalizedString":"The Mitsubishi A6M \"Zero\" was a long-range fighter aircraft, used by the Imperial Japanese Navy from 1940 to 1945. The A6M ZERO was considered one of the best carrier-based fighter aircraft of its time, with excellent maneuverability and a very long range. In the early stages of the war it gained a legendary reputation as a dog fighter and it was not until 1942 that the Allies managed to capture an almost intact Zero and managed to gather intelligence about its strengths and weaknesses. This allowed the Allies to design aircraft to measure up to the Zero, which resulted in the design of the Grummen Hellcat."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Basic","isInPermanentPool":true,"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Deployment","EHelpBubbleTypes::Ambush"],"draftBaseWeight":1.2,"hasDeployment":true,"hasAmbush":true,"soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundCue'AU_Exp_Aircraft_Medium_Cue'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Card_Blowups/AU_Exp_Aircraft_Medium_Cue.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Japan/t_zero_wrobel_close.t_zero_wrobel_close","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Jarosław Wróbel","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/A6M_ZERO.A6M_ZERO","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":241.0},"historyPhotoSource":"https://ww2db.com","historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_zero_photo","SourceString":"A6M3 Model 22 fighter over the Solomon Islands, 1943.","LocalizedString":"A6M3 Model 22 fighter over the Solomon Islands, 1943."},"historyTypeDescription":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_zero_header","SourceString":"Fighter Aircraft","LocalizedString":"Fighter Aircraft"},"blowUpExplosion":{"ObjectName":"ParticleSystem'P_ExplosionAircraftM'